{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1498947-recommendation-for-canonical-chronicles","id":1498947,"title":"Recommendation for canonical chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-06T07:03:41-08:00","id":1498947,"title":"Recommendation for canonical chronicles","content":"White Wolf has published many chronicles these years, some are the whole books (ToJ books, Giovanni Chronicles, Transylvania Chronicles, Under a Blood Red Moon, etc), some are included (City Books, etc). We think about introducing good ones and playing them, but have no idea how to choose","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T13:08:25-08:00","id":1498987,"title":"","content":"It depends of what you want to achieve. Ideas that I used:<br /> <br /> 1. Transylvania by night adventure ideas (for one player, Ventrue, childe of Vencel Rikard from Buda-pest) and some NPCs)-&gt;Clash of Wills (mentioned childe is send to London to learn from Mithras, that's where she met the rest of PCs, created for Ventrue Chronicles, 3 Ventrue, a Gangrel and a Tremere)-&gt;Transylvania Chronicles (the coterie is send there by their Sires). Between parts of TC (looking by the year of each module): Fountains of Bright Crimson, Under the Black Cross and first chapter of Ventrue Chronicles (english characters are called back by prince of York). By the end of XIII century they ruled the fiefs of Galtre (I placed it near Northampton; after Clash of Wills), Leeds (a reward after first chapter of Ventrue Chronicles) and a few in Transylvania (after Transylvania Chronicles). If they would place some NPCs to govern it (and you are good at modding) you could modify Princes of Darkness for Crusader Kings to make downtime more interesting. Then I moved to the Giovanni Chronicles (some players lost their characters, the rest would be NPCs, alternatively you could run it for another group) and they met each other in Silchester during Transylvania Chronicles part II. These two group merged, some characters on the Camarilla side others went with the Sabbat. Later some players move to Ventrue Chronicles chapter 2 as childe of their characters (some characters died, become unplayable or went to sleep), some to Giovanni Chronicles part IV as part of Giovanni clan (so in the end I run my games for 4 groups) and some finished Transylvania Chronicles. It took me about 15 years to achieve that but it was worth it.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2. I started with Blood Nativity. After that one of the characters sided with the Prince the rest either went to Gary or Washington. Those who went to Gary following the advice of R. J (Gangrel from Blood Nativity) went through Baptism of Fire from core rulebook -&gt; Ashes to Ashes -&gt; Dark Tower (White Wolf Magazine 32) -&gt; Blood at Dawn -&gt; Blood Bond -&gt; Miliwaukee by Night -&gt; After the Flood and, finally, Under a Blood Red Moon, with Diablerie Mexico and Succubus Club adventures between them. They sired/adopted a few children during those adventures and that led to Los Angeles or Vancouver (I let my players run 2 characters in different cities, and, as in LA by Night and Vancouver by Night, run those adventures). Those went to Washington (following the suggestion of Isabela Mendes, a Ventrue from Blood Nativity) melt into the big politics (during the adventure ideas from DC by Night), in the meantime met with characters from Giovanni Chronicles part IV and I run a story from Dark Colony for this patchwork group. After that I run Diablerie Britain for them and, as they went to New Orleans for Mardi Gras, an adventure from New Orlean by Night. In The meantime I also run a few adventures for those who wanted to play as the Sabbat. And another 5 years of playing.<br /> <br /> Of course in the meantime I also run my own ideas, but you asked about official sourcebooks. Also, as I run Werewolf: the Apocalypse also, a few times those two groups clashed each other and let me and the players put some fresh blood to my chronicles.<br /> <br /> Of course one of my dreams was to merge those two storylines, add some more of others WoD creatures (and player groups; I think that I could do that) but some of my players married, have children and don't have time for playing, some moved abroad. A few even gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 12-09-2022, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}